                <pb facs="0027" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.N.C./217: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-13T19:00:00-03:00">December 13, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 13—6:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2039. Department’s 1340, December 12 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>], 3 p.m.
                    Professor Fenwick’s message was delivered to Doctor Mello Franco. He will bring
                    the matter before the Committee on December 15. Dr. Franco is of the belief,
                    however, that the Committee cannot extend its functions without the consent of
                    the interested governments. He suggests that this matter be studied at the
                    meeting of Ministers of Foreign Affairs shortly to take place in Rio.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
